// Release index nodes live here, one file per release, named RELEASE.<version>.kdl.
// Semver is the identity, so the <YYMMDD>.<NN> ladder does not apply — same exemption
// as CAP, for the same reason: the name is the meaning (ES.260819.01/E12).
//
// A node is written once at `cut-release` and never edited. It is an INDEX INTO GIT,
// never a copy of what git holds — git is the only clock the record has, and a second
// clock disagrees eventually (ES.260819.01/E21).
//
// Shape:
//
//     release "0.8.0" {
//         tag        "v0.8.0"
//         commit     "abc123…"          // what `verify-published` compares against
//         cut-at     "2026-08-20T12:00:00-05:00"
//         binds      "TS.260820.01" "TS.260820.04"
//         resolves   "S4"               // symptoms this release closed, in FRAME order
//         publishes  "docs/releases/0.8.0/"
//     }
//
// No release has been cut against this frame yet, so this directory holds only its rule.
